WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
Here are two ways to treat
depression that look nothing alike.

2
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:06.000
On the left, a tablet.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:10.290
Its chemical works in the tiny gaps
between nerve cells in the brain.

4
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.030
On the right, two people
in chairs, just talking.

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.530
Week by week, tangled thoughts
start to look clearer.

6
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.580
Doctors often use both.

7
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.960
So why treat depression
with pills and talking?

8
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.680
Wouldn't one be enough?

9
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:30.300
In this mission, you'll see how
antidepressants called SSRIs block reuptake,

10
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.350
so serotonin stays in the synapse longer.

11
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.670
And you'll see how CBT, a talking therapy,

12
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.800
helps people identify and
challenge negative thoughts,

13
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.850
and change what they do.

14
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.030
Your mission: work out why
doctors so often reach for both.
